window.CET6_DATA("data/articles/day-013.json",{"day":13,"title":"Rebuilding More Than a Museum","targetWords":[{"word":"quake","gloss":"地震","context":"After the quake, the town museum stood on the verge of collapse.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"treasury","gloss":"财政部门","context":"A committee responsible to the treasury invited a bank teller, an indigenous craft worker, and a retired bishop to review the proposal.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"accountable","gloss":"负责任的","context":"They wanted officials to be accountable, not merely optimistic.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"bishop","gloss":"主教","context":"A committee responsible to the treasury invited a bank teller, an indigenous craft worker, and a retired bishop to review the proposal.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"brew","gloss":"煮制","context":"When the cafe finally began to brew coffee in a permanent kitchen, the achievement felt earned.","contextParagraph":4,"collocation":null},{"word":"civic","gloss":"公共事务的","context":"The first challenge was practical, but the next was civic: why should scarce public money restore a museum when homes and shops also needed repair?","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"cliche","gloss":"陈词滥调","context":"The director resisted the cliche, and rejected the proverb that disaster inevitably makes a community stronger.","contextParagraph":4,"collocation":null},{"word":"dole","gloss":"救济金","context":"For households dependent on the dole, even a small delay in assistance had consequences that museum supporters needed to acknowledge.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"dub","gloss":"称作","context":"A journalist wanted to dub the project a miracle.","contextParagraph":4,"collocation":null},{"word":"inborn","gloss":"与生俱来的","context":"Nobody claimed that scientific curiosity was wholly inborn.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"midday","gloss":"中午","context":"Volunteers arrived at midday from the local emergency corps.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"pasta","gloss":"意大利面","context":"During a funding crunch, volunteers ran a temporary cafe serving pasta and fresh coffee.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"physiological","gloss":"生理的","context":"A practitioner offered a gentle massage workshop about physiological relaxation, clearly separating it from claims to medical treatment.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"proficient","gloss":"熟练的","context":"A display about optical science let a proficient student explain how an optic nerve carried visual information.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"ridicule","gloss":"嘲笑","context":"The educators agreed not to ridicule a mistaken answer: a person’s intellect was more likely to develop when uncertainty could be expressed safely.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"souvenir","gloss":"纪念品","context":"A buffalo-shaped handicraft stood beside a souvenir from a school tournament.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"teller","gloss":"出纳员","context":"A committee responsible to the treasury invited a bank teller, an indigenous craft worker, and a retired bishop to review the proposal.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"ware","gloss":"家用器物","context":"An old exhibit had praised the monarchy while ignoring the people who cultivated a hectare of land or sold modest household ware.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"bust","gloss":"半身像","context":"A bronze bust lay beside a broken display case, and water threatened to disintegrate a collection of letters.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"dispatch","gloss":"派遣","context":"Some carried a mop; others helped dispatch damaged objects to a storage depot.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"fingerprint","gloss":"指纹","context":"Each fingerprint on a clay tile became a small record of participation, while a single dime donated by a child mattered symbolically as much as a larger gift.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"greed","gloss":"贪婪","context":"The museum’s recovery depended on decisions, resources, and a refusal to let greed determine whose memories survived.","contextParagraph":4,"collocation":null},{"word":"indefinite","gloss":"不确定的","context":"One vendor said that restoring a famous aristocrat’s portrait should not receive indefinite priority over living residents.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"literal","gloss":"字面的","context":"Its name was chosen carefully, avoiding a literal promise of perfection.","contextParagraph":4,"collocation":null},{"word":"massage","gloss":"按摩","context":"A practitioner offered a gentle massage workshop about physiological relaxation, clearly separating it from claims to medical treatment.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"optic","gloss":"视觉的","context":"A display about optical science let a proficient student explain how an optic nerve carried visual information.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"reunite","gloss":"重聚","context":"Residents could reunite with old friends, swap memories, and upload photographs.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"swap","gloss":"交换","context":"Residents could reunite with old friends, swap memories, and upload photographs.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"upload","gloss":"上传","context":"Residents could reunite with old friends, swap memories, and upload photographs.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"vendor","gloss":"小贩","context":"One vendor said that restoring a famous aristocrat’s portrait should not receive indefinite priority over living residents.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"aristocrat","gloss":"贵族","context":"One vendor said that restoring a famous aristocrat’s portrait should not receive indefinite priority over living residents.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"buffalo","gloss":"水牛","context":"A buffalo-shaped handicraft stood beside a souvenir from a school tournament.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"corps","gloss":"队伍","context":"Volunteers arrived at midday from the local emergency corps.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"crunch","gloss":"紧缺","context":"During a funding crunch, volunteers ran a temporary cafe serving pasta and fresh coffee.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"depot","gloss":"仓库","context":"Some carried a mop; others helped dispatch damaged objects to a storage depot.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"dime","gloss":"一角硬币","context":"Each fingerprint on a clay tile became a small record of participation, while a single dime donated by a child mattered symbolically as much as a larger gift.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"disintegrate","gloss":"瓦解","context":"A bronze bust lay beside a broken display case, and water threatened to disintegrate a collection of letters.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"frantic","gloss":"焦虑的","context":"Volunteers heard cups rattle in the surviving hall, while purposeful activity gave frantic residents something practical to do.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"handicraft","gloss":"手工艺品","context":"A buffalo-shaped handicraft stood beside a souvenir from a school tournament.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"hectare","gloss":"公顷","context":"An old exhibit had praised the monarchy while ignoring the people who cultivated a hectare of land or sold modest household ware.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"indigenous","gloss":"原住民的","context":"A committee responsible to the treasury invited a bank teller, an indigenous craft worker, and a retired bishop to review the proposal.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"logo","gloss":"标识","context":"Loss was real; pessimism could not be wished away with a cheerful logo.","contextParagraph":4,"collocation":null},{"word":"monarchy","gloss":"君主政体","context":"An old exhibit had praised the monarchy while ignoring the people who cultivated a hectare of land or sold modest household ware.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"mop","gloss":"拖把","context":"Some carried a mop; others helped dispatch damaged objects to a storage depot.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"pessimism","gloss":"悲观","context":"Loss was real; pessimism could not be wished away with a cheerful logo.","contextParagraph":4,"collocation":null},{"word":"proverb","gloss":"谚语","context":"The director resisted the cliche, and rejected the proverb that disaster inevitably makes a community stronger.","contextParagraph":4,"collocation":null},{"word":"rattle","gloss":"发出嗒嗒声","context":"Volunteers heard cups rattle in the surviving hall, while purposeful activity gave frantic residents something practical to do.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"spaceship","gloss":"宇宙飞船","context":"Nearby, children inspected a model spaceship and asked how astronauts observed distant objects.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"synonym","gloss":"同义词","context":"Nor was resilience a synonym for tolerating neglect.","contextParagraph":4,"collocation":null},{"word":"tournament","gloss":"锦标赛","context":"A buffalo-shaped handicraft stood beside a souvenir from a school tournament.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null}],"paragraphs":[{"en":"After the quake, the town museum stood on the verge of collapse. A bronze bust lay beside a broken display case, and water threatened to disintegrate a collection of letters. Volunteers arrived at midday from the local emergency corps. Some carried a mop; others helped dispatch damaged objects to a storage depot. The first challenge was practical, but the next was civic: why should scarce public money restore a museum when homes and shops also needed repair?","zh":"地震后，城镇博物馆几乎倒塌。一尊青铜半身像倒在破损展柜旁，水正在威胁一批书信，使其可能损毁。中午，地方应急队的志愿者赶来。有些人拿着拖把，有些人帮助把受损物品送到仓库。最初的挑战很实际，接下来却是公共事务问题：住宅和商店也需要修复，为什么要用稀缺公款修复博物馆？"},{"en":"A committee responsible to the treasury invited a bank teller, an indigenous craft worker, and a retired bishop to review the proposal. They wanted officials to be accountable, not merely optimistic. One vendor said that restoring a famous aristocrat’s portrait should not receive indefinite priority over living residents. An old exhibit had praised the monarchy while ignoring the people who cultivated a hectare of land or sold modest household ware. Rebuilding offered a chance to change those priorities rather than reproduce them. For households dependent on the dole, even a small delay in assistance had consequences that museum supporters needed to acknowledge.","zh":"一个向财政部门负责的委员会，邀请银行柜员、原住民手艺人和退休主教审查方案。他们希望官员切实负责，而不只是乐观。一位摊贩说，修复知名贵族的肖像，不应无限期地优先于活着的居民。旧展览曾赞美君主制度，却忽视耕种一公顷土地或出售普通家用品的人。重建提供了改变这些优先次序的机会，而不只是复制原有安排。对于依赖救济金的家庭，援助哪怕延误很短时间，也会造成博物馆支持者必须正视的后果。"},{"en":"The new design linked history to daily experience. A buffalo-shaped handicraft stood beside a souvenir from a school tournament. A display about optical science let a proficient student explain how an optic nerve carried visual information. Nearby, children inspected a model spaceship and asked how astronauts observed distant objects. Nobody claimed that scientific curiosity was wholly inborn. Visitors learned through conversation and experiment, sometimes making errors. The educators agreed not to ridicule a mistaken answer: a person’s intellect was more likely to develop when uncertainty could be expressed safely.","zh":"新设计把历史与日常经验联系起来。水牛造型的手工艺品与学校比赛纪念品并列。光学展台让一名熟练的学生解释视神经如何传递视觉信息。附近，孩子们观察模型飞船，询问宇航员如何观测远方物体。没有人声称科学好奇心完全与生俱来。游客通过交流与实验学习，有时也会犯错。教育人员同意不嘲笑错误答案：能够安心表达不确定时，一个人的思考能力更容易发展。"},{"en":"During a funding crunch, volunteers ran a temporary cafe serving pasta and fresh coffee. Volunteers heard cups rattle in the surviving hall, while purposeful activity gave frantic residents something practical to do. A practitioner offered a gentle massage workshop about physiological relaxation, clearly separating it from claims to medical treatment. Residents could reunite with old friends, swap memories, and upload photographs. Each fingerprint on a clay tile became a small record of participation, while a single dime donated by a child mattered symbolically as much as a larger gift.","zh":"经费紧张时，志愿者开设临时咖啡馆，供应意面和现煮咖啡。志愿者听见杯碟声在尚存的大厅里响起，有意义的忙碌让焦虑的居民有实际的事情可做。一位从业者举办轻柔按摩课程，讲解生理放松，并明确不宣称它属于医疗治疗。居民可以与老朋友重逢、交换记忆、上传照片。泥板上的每枚指纹成为参与的记录；孩子捐的一枚硬币，在象征意义上与大额捐款一样重要。"},{"en":"A journalist wanted to dub the project a miracle. The director resisted the cliche, and rejected the proverb that disaster inevitably makes a community stronger. Loss was real; pessimism could not be wished away with a cheerful logo. Nor was resilience a synonym for tolerating neglect. The museum’s recovery depended on decisions, resources, and a refusal to let greed determine whose memories survived. Its name was chosen carefully, avoiding a literal promise of perfection. When the cafe finally began to brew coffee in a permanent kitchen, the achievement felt earned. Residents continued to debate what deserved public funding, but they now had a place where that disagreement could be expressed alongside the material evidence of their shared history.","zh":"记者想把项目称作奇迹。馆长拒绝这种陈词滥调，也不接受“灾难必然使社区更强大”之类的格言。损失是真实的，漂亮标志无法驱散悲观。韧性也不等同于忍受忽视。博物馆的恢复依赖具体决定、资源投入，以及不让贪婪决定谁的记忆能够保存的坚持。新名称经过谨慎选择，没有在字面上承诺完美。当永久厨房终于能煮咖啡时，这份成果显得来之不易。居民仍在争论什么值得公共资助，但现在有了一个场所，可以在共同历史的实物证据旁表达分歧。"}],"previous":12,"next":14});
